# Acknowledgement list for checkpoint ancestry in redblue `main`.
#
# Audited by `tests/checkpoint_ancestry_test.rs`. Parsed, not skimmed: an
# entry without a `|`-separated reason is rejected, so a SHA cannot be
# recorded without saying why it is tolerated.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# `rbops/dispatch.sh` resumes an interrupted phase with a real `git merge`, so
# a phase checkpointed mid-flight reached `main` without passing the reviewer.
# The commits below are those checkpoints. All of them carry code that no human
# reviewed.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* DONE
# Published history is not rewritten. No rebase, no filter-branch, no reset, no
# amend of an already-published commit. No force-push is attempted by this file,
# by the audit, or by any gate - AGENTS.md §1.6 forbids it. Erasing these
# commits would make the audit green by destroying the evidence, which is the
# opposite of what it is for.
#
# WHAT TO DO IF A NEW ONE APPEARS
# A new line here means somebody has looked at what the commit introduced and
# decided it can stay. A new commit WITHOUT a line here fails the audit.

# --- rbops: phase-NNN checkpoint commits in main's ancestry -----------------
#
# Each reached main through `Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/rbops-wip/...'`
# (see wip_merges_on_main below). dispatch.sh now resumes with
# `git merge --squash`, so that path is closed; these six predate it.

7fdea15f13a0cc2021c5cc69a65a126879e2d554|phase-019 checkpoint, tolerated: published via a resume merge that the reviewer never saw. Code is in examples/ and bootstrap/ only; no language semantics or public type changed. Recorded rather than rewritten.
074c95e24fbf8b1101219bc1f10c520d8b7acd24|phase-019 checkpoint, tolerated: the earlier of the two phase-019 checkpoints, superseded by 7fdea15. Nothing reviewed; kept only so main's ancestry stays intact.
563a3513c7fba2d2a39e759632415fef4bb60eb5|phase-018 checkpoint, tolerated: published via a resume merge that the reviewer never saw. No language semantics or public type changed. Recorded rather than rewritten.
286fccd537d963cb9ad1bcbb051bce45d537a683|phase-016 checkpoint, tolerated: published via a resume merge that the reviewer never saw. No language semantics or public type changed. Recorded rather than rewritten.
32d52ad3d50859c97db57dd10542c653f9962ea4|phase-004 checkpoint, tolerated: the oldest checkpoint on main, below the boundary the original finding's `git log` could reach, so the finding undercounted it. Recorded rather than rewritten.
97b4043cd92e7b2b8a7511a6600b8e73ba9d2596|phase-004 checkpoint, tolerated: the earlier of the two phase-004 checkpoints, superseded by 32d52ad. Recorded rather than rewritten.

# --- The recurrence path, measured separately ------------------------------
#
# `Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/rbops-wip/...'` commits on main. This is
# the route by which the six checkpoints above were published. dispatch.sh now
# resumes with `git merge --squash`, which creates no merge commit, so this
# number can only move if something merges a wip branch onto main again.
#
# Raising it deliberately is fine: add the sha to the list above with a reason,
# then bump this number in the same commit. The audit fails until you do.

wip_merges_on_main=6
